        "summary": {
            "abstract": "Generation Scotland (Scottish Family Health Study) is an intensively phenotyped, family-based cohort for the study of the genetic basis of common complex diseases and response to treatments. This record covers the 2015 genotyping: DNA from over 20,000 GS:SFHS participants analysed by high-density genome-wide chip genotyping (Illumina OmniExpress SNP GWAS, 700k) and exome chip (250K).",
